# Credentials for `bin/sciebo setup`.
#
# This file is optional: `bin/sciebo setup --login` authenticates through the
# Nextcloud Login Flow in your browser and needs no app password here. Use
# this file to provide the credentials by hand, non-interactively.
#
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill in the three values, or just
# run `bin/sciebo setup` and answer its prompts.
#
# SCIEBO_URL
#   Base URL of your institution's sciebo instance, for example
#   https://uni-muenster.sciebo.de (see the server list:
#   https://docs.sciebo.de/docs/getting-started/webinterface/serverliste/).
#   `setup` turns it into https://<host>/remote.php/dav/files/<user>/, which
#   Nextcloud chunked uploads require.
#
# SCIEBO_USER
#   Your sciebo ID in <localid>@<scope> form, for example
#   alice@uni-muenster.de.
#
# SCIEBO_APP_PASSWORD
#   An app password from Settings > Security > Devices & sessions. Required
#   when two-factor authentication is enabled, and recommended for any
#   third-party client. Never put your main sciebo password here. `setup`
#   stores it in the platform Keychain by default (KEYCHAIN=1); with KEYCHAIN=0
#   or --no-keychain it is obscured into the rclone config instead.

SCIEBO_URL=""
SCIEBO_USER=""
SCIEBO_APP_PASSWORD=""
